{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder_test.cljc | sed -n '230,335p'; rg -n \\\"defn mint-oldest|defn cursor-entry|defn .*park\\\" src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   230\t  [pb]\n   231\t  (::resp/endpoint @(:responder pb)))\n   232\t\n   233\t\n   234\t;; =============================================================================\n   235\t;; Peer A: reflections and a real VM over them\n   236\t;; =============================================================================\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn- peer-a\n   239\t  [a-end]\n   240\t  (let [events (ring 1024)]\n   241\t    {:events events\n   242\t     :attach! (remote/attacher {:dao.stream.remote/channels {chan a-end}\n   243\t                                :dao.stream.remote/events events})}))\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\t(defn- reflect\n   247\t  [pa descriptor]\n   248\t  (:dao.stream/handle ((:attach! pa) descriptor)))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- poll!\n   252\t  \"Ask `f` until it answers something other than blocked or retry,\n   253\t   driving B between asks.\"\n   254\t  [pb f]\n   255\t  (loop [n 0]\n   256\t    (let [r (f)]\n   257\t      (if (and (< n 12)\n   258\t               (or (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   259\t                   (:dao.stream/retry? r)))\n   260\t        (do (drive! pb) (recur (inc n)))\n   261\t        r))))\n   262\t\n   263\t\n   264\t(def ^:private secret \"yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.responder-test/secret\")\n   265\t\n   266\t\n   267\t(def ^:private load-ast\n   268\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader (linearize/ast-loader semantic/vm-load-program)\n   269\t                        vm/ast-contract))\n   270\t\n   271\t\n   272\t(defn- make-ring-stream\n   273\t  [capacity]\n   274\t  (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n   275\t                       :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity}))\n   276\t\n   277\t\n   278\t(defn- remote-vm\n   279\t  \"A real semantic VM on peer A whose FFI call pair is two reflections\n   280\t   of B's served endpoint, and NO bridge: every call it makes is\n   281\t   answered at B or not at all. call-in is seen through `seen`, which\n   282\t   notes each value the VM appends. The call-out cursor the VM mints\n   283\t   at construction is asked for first, B driven until it is filed.\"\n   284\t  [pa pb seen]\n   285\t  (let [ep (endpoint pb)\n   286\t        in (reflect pa (apply2/endpoint-request ep))\n   287\t        out (reflect pa (apply2/endpoint-response ep))]\n   288\t    (poll! pb #(stream/cursor out :dao.stream/oldest))\n   289\t    {:in in, :out out,\n   290\t     :vm (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream make-ring-stream\n   291\t                              :capability-secret secret\n   292\t                              :call-in (recording in seen)\n   293\t                              :call-out out})}))\n   294\t\n   295\t\n   296\t(defn- lit\n   297\t  [v]\n   298\t  {:type :literal, :value v})\n   299\t\n   300\t\n   301\t(defn- call-node\n   302\t  [op & args]\n   303\t  {:type :dao.stream.apply/call, :op op, :operands (mapv lit args)})\n   304\t\n   305\t\n   306\t(defn- load-call\n   307\t  [machine ast]\n   308\t  (load-ast machine (vm/ast->datoms ast)))\n   309\t\n   310\t\n   311\t(defn- settle\n   312\t  \"Run `machine` until it halts or 12 drive rounds pass.\"\n   313\t  [pb machine]\n   314\t  (loop [v (vm/run machine)\n   315\t         n 0]\n   316\t    (if (and (vm/blocked? v) (< n 12))\n   317\t      (do (drive! pb) (recur (vm/run v) (inc n)))\n   318\t      v)))\n   319\t\n   320\t\n   321\t(defn- raised\n   322\t  \"The exception `thunk` raised, or nil.\"\n   323\t  [thunk]\n   324\t  (try (thunk) nil\n   325\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e e)))\n   326\t\n   327\t\n   328\t(defn- apply-error\n   329\t  \"The portable apply error `call-result` raised, found on `e` or its\n   330\t   causes.\"\n   331\t  [e]\n   332\t  (loop [e e]\n   333\t    (when e\n   334\t      (or (:error (ex-data e))\n   335\t          (recur (ex-cause e))))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:1488:(defn park-continuation\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:530:(defn mint-oldest\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:547:(defn cursor-entry\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder.cljc | sed -n '1,220p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/holder.cljc | sed -n '185,235p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder.cljc | sed -n '1,220p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/holder.cljc | sed -n '185,235p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.responder\n     2\t  \"The FFI apply responder at the possessing peer: the interpreter that\n     3\t   reads apply requests off a VM's call-in stream and appends apply\n     4\t   responses to its call-out stream, over the call pair an export\n     5\t   binding (`yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve`) serves to a remote VM.\n     6\t\n     7\t   It is a separate namespace because it is a separate observer of the\n     8\t   same streams. The binding's mirror serves stream OPERATIONS on\n     9\t   call-in and call-out -- a remote VM's append! lands on call-in, its\n    10\t   next reads call-out -- and interprets no value; this responder\n    11\t   interprets the apply VALUES and knows nothing of the channel, the\n    12\t   table or the leases. Neither drives the other: the one drive owner\n    13\t   calls `rs/step` and `step` in turn.\n    14\t\n    15\t   `open!` exports call-in as a remote WRITER and call-out as a remote\n    16\t   READER through the binding's own `serve!`, so the binding's\n    17\t   injected authority gate (`::rs/admit?`) and surface policy decide\n    18\t   whether this peer's handlers are reachable at all -- there is no\n    19\t   second, default gate that admits everything. The handler map is\n    20\t   required and explicit.\n    21\t\n    22\t   `step` is one `dao.stream.apply/serve-once!` over the caller-owned\n    23\t   server state the responder value carries: the request is read\n    24\t   whole, as the VM appended it -- extra keys and all, never rebuilt\n    25\t   from op and args -- its id answered on call-out, and a computed\n    26\t   response retained with its successor across `full`, so no handler\n    27\t   runs twice. Two responder-level rules sit on top:\n    28\t\n    29\t   - A gap on the call-in cursor is terminal loss (as\n    30\t     `yin.vm.ffi/bridge-step` treats it locally): a request was evicted\n    31\t     and the parked call that made it could never be answered. The\n    32\t     responder reports `::request-lost` and closes call-out, so every\n    33\t     VM waiting on that pair reads end and raises through\n    34\t     `yin.vm.ffi/call-result` instead of parking forever.\n    35\t   - Once the binding no longer serves call-in or call-out -- retired,\n    36\t     closed, or reclaimed by its lease -- the responder is terminal\n    37\t     (`::retired`) and invokes no further handler for that tenure.\n    38\t\n    39\t   The responder is a plain value threaded by its drive owner; nothing\n    40\t   here loops, waits or reads a clock.\"\n    41\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    42\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    43\t            [yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve :as rs]))\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\t(defn- handlers?\n    47\t  \"An explicit handler map: operation keyword -> function.\"\n    48\t  [m]\n    49\t  (and (map? m)\n    50\t       (every? keyword? (keys m))\n    51\t       (every? fn? (vals m))))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn remote-descriptor\n    55\t  \"The portable remote descriptor for a served marker `{:dao.stream/identity\n    56\t   id :dao.stream/channel cd}` -- what a remote peer attaches.\"\n    57\t  [served]\n    58\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n    59\t   :dao.stream/identity (:dao.stream/identity served)\n    60\t   :dao.stream/channel (:dao.stream/channel served)})\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\t(defn- refused\n    64\t  [option reason]\n    65\t  {::status ::refused, ::refusals [{::option option, ::reason reason}]})\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn- served-surface\n    69\t  [binding served]\n    70\t  (get-in (rs/table binding) [(:dao.stream/identity served) :surface]))\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\t(defn- export\n    74\t  \"Serve call-in and call-out through `binding`, or name the refusal.\n    75\t   Returns `[in out nil]` or `[_ _ refusal]`.\"\n    76\t  [binding call-in call-out]\n    77\t  (let [in (rs/serve! binding call-in)\n    78\t        out (when in (rs/serve! binding call-out))]\n    79\t    [in out\n    80\t     (cond\n    81\t       (nil? in) (refused ::call-in ::unservable)\n    82\t       (not (contains? (served-surface binding in) :writer))\n    83\t       (refused ::call-in ::surface)\n    84\t       (nil? out) (refused ::call-out ::unservable)\n    85\t       (not (contains? (served-surface binding out) :reader))\n    86\t       (refused ::call-out ::surface))]))\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t(defn open!\n    90\t  \"Export the call pair `::call-in`/`::call-out` through `binding` and\n    91\t   assemble the responder over `::handlers`, or refuse.\n    92\t\n    93\t   `opts`:\n    94\t     ::call-in   the VM's call-in stream at this peer: this responder\n    95\t                 reads it locally, a remote VM appends to it -- served\n    96\t                 with a surface containing :writer\n    97\t     ::call-out  the VM's call-out stream at this peer: this responder\n    98\t                 appends to it, a remote VM reads it -- served with a\n    99\t                 surface containing :reader\n   100\t     ::handlers  the explicit handler map, op keyword -> fn; no default\n   101\t\n   102\t   The request cursor is minted from call-in itself before anything is\n   103\t   served. A refusal -- no handler map, a call-in that mints no\n   104\t   cursor, either endpoint unservable under the binding's gate and\n   105\t   surface policy, or served without the surface it needs -- retires\n   106\t   every identity this call served, so no provisional export outlives\n   107\t   it; handles already served before it stay served.\n   108\t\n   109\t   Returns `{::binding b ::call-in h ::call-out h ::handlers m\n   110\t   ::endpoint apply-endpoint ::state apply-server-state}` --\n   111\t   `::endpoint` is the `dao.stream.apply/endpoint` of the two remote\n   112\t   descriptors a remote VM attaches -- or `{::status ::refused\n   113\t   ::refusals [...]}`.\"\n   114\t  [binding {::keys [call-in call-out handlers]}]\n   115\t  (cond\n   116\t    (not (rs/binding? binding)) (refused ::binding ::malformed)\n   117\t    (nil? handlers) (refused ::handlers ::missing)\n   118\t    (not (handlers? handlers)) (refused ::handlers ::malformed)\n   119\t    (not (stream/reader? call-in)) (refused ::call-in ::malformed)\n   120\t    (not (stream/writer? call-out)) (refused ::call-out ::malformed)\n   121\t    :else\n   122\t    (let [c (stream/cursor call-in :dao.stream/oldest)]\n   123\t      (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome c))\n   124\t        (refused ::call-in ::no-cursor)\n   125\t        (let [before (into #{} (map :identity) (rs/entries binding))\n   126\t              [in out refusal] (export binding call-in call-out)]\n   127\t          (if refusal\n   128\t            (do (doseq [e (rs/entries binding)]\n   129\t                  (when-not (contains? before (:identity e))\n   130\t                    (rs/retire! binding (:identity e))))\n   131\t                refusal)\n   132\t            {::binding binding\n   133\t             ::call-in call-in\n   134\t             ::call-out call-out\n   135\t             ::handlers handlers\n   136\t             ::served {::call-in in, ::call-out out}\n   137\t             ::endpoint (apply2/endpoint (remote-descriptor in)\n   138\t                                         (remote-descriptor out))\n   139\t             ::state (apply2/server-state (:dao.stream/cursor c))}))))))\n   140\t\n   141\t\n   142\t(defn- still-served?\n   143\t  [r]\n   144\t  (let [b (::binding r)]\n   145\t    (and (rs/served? b (get-in r [::served ::call-in :dao.stream/identity]))\n   146\t         (rs/served? b (get-in r [::served ::call-out :dao.stream/identity])))))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t(defn- close-call-out!\n   150\t  [r]\n   151\t  (let [out (::call-out r)]\n   152\t    (when (stream/closable? out)\n   153\t      (stream/close! out))))\n   154\t\n   155\t\n   156\t(defn step\n   157\t  \"One responder pass: at most one request read and one response\n   158\t   append (`dao.stream.apply/serve-once!`). Returns serve-once!'s own\n   159\t   result -- `:dao.stream.apply/outcome` and its extra keys -- with the\n   160\t   responder carrying the new state under `::responder`; the drive\n   161\t   owner threads that value into its next `step`.\n   162\t\n   163\t   Outcomes beyond serve-once!'s: `::request-lost` when the call-in\n   164\t   cursor gaps (call-out is closed, the responder terminal), and\n   165\t   `::retired` when the binding no longer serves the pair. Once\n   166\t   terminal, every step answers `:dao.stream.apply/terminal` and\n   167\t   invokes nothing.\"\n   168\t  [r]\n   169\t  (let [s (::state r)\n   170\t        with (fn [result s']\n   171\t               (assoc result ::responder (assoc r ::state s')))]\n   172\t    (cond\n   173\t      (:terminal s)\n   174\t      (with {:dao.stream.apply/outcome :dao.stream.apply/terminal} s)\n   175\t\n   176\t      (not (still-served? r))\n   177\t      (with {:dao.stream.apply/outcome ::retired}\n   178\t            (assoc s :terminal ::retired))\n   179\t\n   180\t      :else\n   181\t      (let [result (apply2/serve-once! (::handlers r) (::call-in r)\n   182\t                                       (::call-out r) s)\n   183\t            s' (:dao.stream.apply/state result)]\n   184\t        (if (= :dao.stream.apply/gap (:dao.stream.apply/outcome result))\n   185\t          (do (close-call-out! r)\n   186\t              (with (assoc result :dao.stream.apply/outcome ::request-lost)\n   187\t                    (assoc s' :terminal ::request-lost)))\n   188\t          (with result s'))))))\n   185\t        (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   186\t        (assoc h ::grants-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   187\t        (gone? r) (assoc h ::reclaimed? true)\n   188\t        :else h))))\n   189\t\n   190\t\n   191\t(defn- my-grant?\n   192\t  [h v]\n   193\t  (and (lease/lease-fact? v)\n   194\t       (= :dao.lease/accepted (:dao.lease/status v))\n   195\t       (= (::subject h) (:dao.lease/subject v))))\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t(defn- assemble\n   199\t  \"This subject's `grant` was read at the grants cursor: attach the\n   200\t   renewal medium it names, assemble make-holder with the holder\n   201\t   identity it names, and observe the grant at the latest reading. Nil\n   202\t   when the grant cannot be held yet -- no reading, or no attachment --\n   203\t   so the caller re-reads it on a later pass.\"\n   204\t  [h grant]\n   205\t  (when-some [renewal (attach (::attach! h)\n   206\t                              {:dao.stream/identity (:dao.lease/holder grant)\n   207\t                               :dao.stream/channel (::channel h)})]\n   208\t    (let [composed (lease/make-holder\n   209\t                     (holder-config h (::grants h) (::grants-cursor h)\n   210\t                                    (:dao.lease/holder grant) renewal))\n   211\t          holder (lease/observe-grant (:holder composed) rs/grantor\n   212\t                                      grant (::reading h))]\n   213\t      (when (some? (:grant holder))\n   214\t        (assoc h ::composed composed ::renewal renewal ::holder holder)))))\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t(defn- seek-grant\n   218\t  \"Read `lease-grants` up to the budget for this subject's grant.\"\n   219\t  [h]\n   220\t  (let [h (mint-grants-cursor h)]\n   221\t    (if (or (::reclaimed? h) (nil? (::grants-cursor h)))\n   222\t      h\n   223\t      (loop [h h\n   224\t             n (::budget h)]\n   225\t        (if (zero? n)\n   226\t          h\n   227\t          (let [r (stream/next (::grants h) (::grants-cursor h))]\n   228\t            (cond\n   229\t              (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   230\t              (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)\n   231\t                    c' (:dao.stream/cursor r)]\n   232\t                (if (my-grant? h v)\n   233\t                  (if-some [h' (assemble h v)]\n   234\t                    (assoc h' ::grants-cursor c')\n   235\t                    h)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The collision is only part of the failure. Each VM has one call-out cursor, and the current wait sweep can hand a response for another call to the wrong waiter. I’m tracing that sweep before choosing the ID shape, since a new ID alone would turn the wrong result into a correlation error."}}
